# **Magic Words list / explanation:**  
# — “Close / Complete / Resolve” kinds (will mark the issue as Done upon merge):  
#   close, closes, closed, closing  
#   fix, fixes, fixed, fixing  
#   resolve, resolves, resolved, resolving  
#   complete, completes, completed, completing  
#  
# — “Reference / relate / mention” kinds (will *not* automatically close the issue):  
#   ref, references  
#   part of  
#   related to  
#   contributes to  
#   towards  
#  
# Example uses:  
#   Closes LINEAR-1234  
#   Fixes LINEAR-5678  
#   Resolves LINEAR-9012  
#   References LINEAR-3456  
#   Related to LINEAR-7890  
#  
# **Breaking changes (Breaking Change) should be indicated like this:**  
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <description of breaking change>  
# Or put “!” after the type (e.g. feat!, refactor!) to indicate a breaking change  
#  
# **Multiple issue / PR associations**  
# If a commit involves multiple Linear issues, you can write multiple magic-word lines, for example:  
#   Closes LINEAR-1234  
#   Fixes LINEAR-2345  
#   Related to LINEAR-3456  
#  
# **PR / Issue reference relationships**  
# In addition to putting magic words in the commit message, you can also use the same magic words + issue ID in PR titles or descriptions to trigger linking.

